WEBVTT

NOTE
The film carries no speech — it is a silent screen recording under music, with
on-screen caption pills. These cues mirror those pills plus what is happening on
screen, so the demo is usable with sound off, by screen reader, and is indexable.

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.700
Braid — every AI you already pay for. One question. One table.

2
00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:08.000
A question is typed once: "Ask once. Every mind you pay for weighs in."

3
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.900
Every seat answers — Claude, Grok, Gemini, ChatGPT and a local Adam seat.

4
00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.700
Three ways to read the room.

5
00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:21.300
Side by side, stacked, or one thread — the same answers, three layouts.

6
00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:23.800
Flows — presets, or draw who answers whom: roles, sequential peers,
adversarial teams, Socratic drill, steelman relay.

7
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:26.900
Loops — run it once, N laps, or until it reaches a goal.

8
00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:31.500
Permissions — per seat, what context it sees and whether it can touch files.

9
00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:34.000
Now make them fight.

10
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:43.900
An adversarial round: builders versus attackers, each seat hunting a real flaw
in the design the table just committed to, with live handoffs between seats.

11
00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:47.800
Braid — open beta, ten dollars a month. Your subscriptions, your machine,
nothing proxied.
